# ==============================================================================
# Query Name: 01_event_type_distribution.spl
# Project: P1 — Splunk SOC Home Lab & Log Analysis
# Purpose: Summarize security events by categorization
# Security Use Case: Authentication health monitoring and initial attack surface triage
# ==============================================================================

index=main 
| stats count by event_type 
| sort - count

# Expected Interpretation:
# - Quantifies distribution across:
#   * Successful SSH Login
#   * Failed SSH Login
#   * Multiple Failed Authentication Attempts
#   * Connection Without Authentication
# - In a baseline environment, successful logins should dominate. A high proportion
#   of failed or multi-attempt events (>50%) indicates active adversary activity.
